WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.163
The alert check.

2
00:00:01.163 --> 00:00:04.664
CISA's baseline under B
O D twenty-five oh-one

3
00:00:04.664 --> 00:00:07.975
asks for two alerts the
role files don't set.

4
00:00:07.975 --> 00:00:12.037
M S A A D seven point seven:
an alert on every eligible

5
00:00:12.037 --> 00:00:16.775
or active assignment to the
eight highly privileged roles.

6
00:00:16.775 --> 00:00:21.663
And seven point eight: an alert on
every Global Administrator activation.

7
00:00:21.663 --> 00:00:25.550
So a separate script reads them
under its own read-only task,

8
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.613
pim alerts, and changes nothing.

9
00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:31.663
Pim ten and pim eleven check each
role's notification settings.

10
00:00:31.663 --> 00:00:34.721
Pim twelve and pim thirteen
check the PIM for Groups

11
00:00:34.721 --> 00:00:38.063
member policy of each group
that holds one of those roles.

12
00:00:38.063 --> 00:00:43.468
Each is a finding until an additional
recipient, the security monitoring mailbox,

13
00:00:43.468 --> 00:00:46.887
is set: under the role's role
settings, notifications,

14
00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:50.862
or the group's PIM for Groups
settings, member, notifications.

15
00:00:50.862 --> 00:00:53.150
PIM's default recipients don't count.

16
00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.588
On the fictional tenant,
all eleven are findings.

17
00:00:56.588 --> 00:01:00.600
Its tests are a separate suite,
in the baseline tests folder.
